Sure, here is a basic example of a KickLang server using Express and MySQL for storage:

```javascript
import express from 'express';
import mysql from 'mysql';
import bodyParser from 'body-parser';
import { compile } from 'kicklang';

// Create the Express app
const app = express();

// Use body parser middleware
app.use(bodyParser.json());

// Connect to the MySQL database
const db = mysql.createConnection({
  host: 'localhost',
  user: 'yourusername',
  password: '<PASSWORD>',
  database: 'yourdatabase'
});

db.connect();

// Define the data model
interface Code74k {
  key: string;
  value: string;
}

// KickLang compiler options
const options = {
  functions: {
    // Custom function to retrieve all Code74k entries
    getAllCode74k: () => {
      return new Promise((resolve, reject) => {
        db.query('SELECT * FROM code74k', (error, results) => {
          if (error) {
            reject(error);
          } else {
            resolve(results);
          }
        });
      });
    },

    // Custom function to create a new Code74k entry
    createCode74k: (key: string, value: string) => {
      return new Promise((resolve, reject) => {
        db.query('INSERT INTO code74k SET ?', { key, value }, (error, result) => {
          if (error) {
            reject(error);
          } else {
            resolve(result);
          }
        });
      });
    },
  }
};

// Compile the KickLang source code
const kicklangCode = `
  rule get_all_code74k {
    when getAllCode74k() -> ?output {
      output = it;
    }
  }

  rule create_code74k {
    when createCode74k($key, $value) -> ?output {
      output = "Entry created successfully";
    }
  }
`;

const { get_all_code74k, create_code74k } = compile(kicklangCode, options);

// Define API endpoints
app.get('/code74k', async (req, res) => {
  try {
    const result = await get_all_code74k();
    res.json(result);
  } catch (error) {
    res.status(500).send(error);
  }
});

app.post('/code74k', async (req, res) => {
  const { key, value } = req.body;
  try {
    await create_code74k(key, value);
    res.send('Entry created successfully');
  } catch (error) {
    res.status(500).send(error);
  }
});

// Start the server
app.listen(3000, () => {
  console.log('Server started on port 3000');
});
```

In this example, we have an Express server that uses MySQL as the data storage. We define two endpoints: one to retrieve all Code74k entries and another to create a new Code74k entry.

The `get_all_code74k` rule uses the `getAllCode74k` custom function to retrieve all entries from the database and return them as the output.

The `create_code74k` rule uses the `createCode74k` custom function to insert a new entry into the database.

You would need to replace `'yourusername'`, `'yourpassword'`, and `'yourdatabase'` with your actual MySQL credentials and database name.

This is a basic example, and you can extend it further by adding more rules, functions, and endpoints as per your requirements.
